# Shell scripts and process-manager configs must reach Linux with LF endings.
#
# `git archive` on a Windows checkout applies core.autocrlf, so these files were
# arriving on the droplet with CRLF. bash then fails on the carriage return
# ("\r: command not found"), which would break the deploy wrapper itself. The
# same defect is already sitting in supervisor.conf.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
